From 31d73e3e829d33a7ca9a2f160cc9b9627f9a809b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:51:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: SKIP_REPORT_METRICS defaults to 1 in bazel-orfs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

bazel-orfs's flows skip the expensive metrics by default: a timing
update, a power analysis and the text reports at every stage that calls
report_metrics, at no benefit to the netlist. The free metrics (0157)
and the tools' own counters are still written. A flow that wants the
timing and power numbers in its stage .json sets SKIP_REPORT_METRICS=0.

bazel-orfs policy, not for upstream. Retires with 0157, or when an
ORFS bump changes the default itself.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 docs/user/FlowVariables.md  | 2 +-
 flow/scripts/variables.json | 2 +-
 flow/scripts/variables.yaml | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/user/FlowVariables.md b/docs/user/FlowVariables.md
index 8262505..149dd87 100644
--- a/docs/user/FlowVariables.md
+++ b/docs/user/FlowVariables.md
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@ configuration file.
 | <a name="SKIP_LAST_GASP"></a>SKIP_LAST_GASP| Do not use last gasp optimization to fix timing violations (default: use gate last gasp).| |
 | <a name="SKIP_PIN_SWAP"></a>SKIP_PIN_SWAP| Do not use pin swapping as a transform to fix timing violations (default: use pin swapping).| |
 | <a name="SKIP_REPAIR_TIE_FANOUT"></a>SKIP_REPAIR_TIE_FANOUT| Skip repair_tie_fanout at floorplan step.| 0|
-| <a name="SKIP_REPORT_METRICS"></a>SKIP_REPORT_METRICS| If set to 1, report_metrics writes only the metrics that cost no analysis: design area, instance counts and utilization. Timing, power, clock skew, the max slew/cap/fanout checks and the reports/<stage>_*.rpt text reports are skipped; they need a timing update and a power analysis at every stage that calls it. The counters the tools record as they run (placement, legalization, routing, repair, warnings) are written either way.| 0|
+| <a name="SKIP_REPORT_METRICS"></a>SKIP_REPORT_METRICS| If set to 1, report_metrics writes only the metrics that cost no analysis: design area, instance counts and utilization. Timing, power, clock skew, the max slew/cap/fanout checks and the reports/<stage>_*.rpt text reports are skipped; they need a timing update and a power analysis at every stage that calls it. The counters the tools record as they run (placement, legalization, routing, repair, warnings) are written either way.| 1|
 | <a name="SKIP_VT_SWAP"></a>SKIP_VT_SWAP| Do not perform VT swap to improve QoR (default: do VT swap).| |
 | <a name="SLEW_MARGIN"></a>SLEW_MARGIN| Specifies a slew margin when fixing max slew violations. This option allows you to overfix.| |
 | <a name="SWAP_ARITH_OPERATORS"></a>SWAP_ARITH_OPERATORS| Improve timing QoR by swapping ALU and MULT arithmetic operators.| 0|
diff --git a/flow/scripts/variables.json b/flow/scripts/variables.json
index 47d0f46..d00272c 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/variables.json
+++ b/flow/scripts/variables.json
@@ -1266,7 +1266,7 @@
     ]
   },
   "SKIP_REPORT_METRICS": {
-    "default": 0,
+    "default": 1,
     "description": "If set to 1, report_metrics writes only the metrics that cost no analysis: design area, instance counts and utilization. Timing, power, clock skew, the max slew/cap/fanout checks and the reports/<stage>_*.rpt text reports are skipped; they need a timing update and a power analysis at every stage that calls it. The counters the tools record as they run (placement, legalization, routing, repair, warnings) are written either way.\n",
     "stages": [
       "synth",
diff --git a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
index fd8387a..e2d2f80 100644
--- a/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
+++ b/flow/scripts/variables.yaml
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ SKIP_REPORT_METRICS:
     - grt
     - route
     - final
-  default: 0
+  default: 1
 PROCESS:
   description: |
     Technology node or process in use.
-- 
